      "writtenOn": "2025-07-28T15:24:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A little more info, it seems that the locks are process level. So all threads can access the file regardless of locks since the thread is running in a process that can access the lock. Thus since we only have one process running at a time it would follow that locks essentially do nothing for us and we should be fine to ignore them? Let me know if that makes sense.",
      "parentUuid": "68388beb_9e16e708",
      "revId": "4ece581ebaf4977621f4a9c018d0b88129301643",
